BaseOS for the Miyoo Flip
=========================

Derived from BaseOS for Allwinner H700 handhelds by Prashant Vaibhav:

    https://github.com/pvaibhav/BaseOS

Forked at commit dbe5211 ("docs: update README.md", 2026-08-15). The full upstream
history is preserved in this repository's git history; upstream authorship is intact
on every commit that carries it.

Files that remain upstream's work, unmodified or nearly so:

    src/fbsplash.c              the framebuffer splash renderer
    src/gptgrow.c               first-boot expand-to-fill; rewritten to read the
                                GPT geometry from the header instead of hardcoding
                                the H700 layout
    src/gptslot.c               A/B slot arithmetic; rewritten around this card's
                                three slotted regions and header-derived geometry
    src/gpt.h                   the CRC and entry helpers both of them share
    tools/mkupdate.py           update payload builder; extended to three regions
    overlay/usr/sbin/baseos-update
                                the update engine, adapted to this layout
    assets/bootlogo.bmp         the BaseOS wordmark
    tools/common.sh             container platform selection
    flash-card.sh               macOS card writer; reduced to one target, and its
                                disk guard rekeyed on removable and virtual media

Taken later, from upstream commit 7dec5cb (2026-09-18):

    overlay/usr/sbin/baseos-config
                                the baseos.conf parser; reduced to hostname and
                                ssh_password, with a fixed default hostname
    assets/baseos.conf          its template
    tests/test-baseos-config.sh its tests, adapted to the above
    overlay/usr/sbin/baseos-mdns
                                starts and stops avahi-daemon on DHCP events
    overlay/etc/avahi/avahi-daemon.conf
    tests/test-baseos-mdns.sh   its tests, run against our udhcpc script
    build-avahi.sh              the static avahi-daemon recipe, from upstream's
                                build-tools.sh

assets/boot.ttf is licensed under the SIL Open Font License; see assets/OFL.txt.

Everything else — the Rockchip boot chain, the SPI NAND preloader work, the my355
rootfs, overlay and documentation — is new in this repository.

BUILT FROM SOURCE
-----------------

/usr/sbin/avahi-daemon is built by build-avahi.sh from unmodified avahi 0.8 and
libdaemon 0.14, both LGPL-2.1, linked statically with musl (MIT), expat (MIT) and
libevent (BSD). The script pins each source by URL and SHA-256, so the binary can
be rebuilt, or relinked against a modified library, from those sources.

VENDOR FIRMWARE
---------------

BaseOS links against the vendor's own userland rather than rebuilding it, and boots
the vendor's own U-Boot and kernel. Three artifacts are therefore vendor-derived:

    uboot.img           Miyoo's Rockchip U-Boot FIT, used verbatim
    boot.img            Miyoo's Android boot image; only the DTB and the logo are
                        rewritten, and the kernel is stored gzipped — the build
                        asserts it decompresses to the vendor bytes
    stock-harvest.tar   79 allowlisted paths from the stock squashfs — glibc,
                        Mali, SDL2, wpa_supplicant, BlueZ, firmware blobs
                        (manifest/harvest.list; the count is in source.json)

None of them is committed to this repository. They are published as a release
artifact by cache-pack.sh and pinned by hash from manifest/prepared/, and
prepare-stock.sh regenerates the identical bytes from a dump of your own unit.

Publishing that bundle redistributes Miyoo's firmware. Miyoo has not granted
permission to do so, and parts of it are third-party works under their own terms
(the Linux kernel is GPL-2.0 and its source has not been published for this build;
glibc is LGPL; the Mali userspace is ARM proprietary).

